  "name_zh_from_listing": "Health54_癌症篩檢--子宮頸抹片篩檢檔(20250624起適用)",
  "data_description_en": "1. Since ROC year 99 (2010) the Health Promotion Administration has expanded screening for four cancers (colorectal, oral, breast and cervical): colorectal, breast, cervical and oral cancer screening is offered through medical institutions contracted for NHI preventive health services, colorectal and oral cancer screening were added to the preventive health service items, and breast cancer screening was extended to women aged 40 to under 45 at high risk through a second-degree relative (mother, daughter, sister, or paternal or maternal grandmother) who has had breast cancer. 2. The government funds one free Pap smear a year for women aged 30 and over and recommends at least one Pap smear every 3 years. The high-risk group includes sexually experienced women; those who married early, have had many children or have had several sexual partners in particular need regular follow-up. 3. Case master file (MASTER): basic data of each case. Smear file (SMEAR): one record per Pap smear; one ID can have several records. 4. Data years span 2004 to 2025.",
  "notes_en": "1. The patient basic information file (H_BHP_PST_MASTER) and smear test data file (H_BHP_PST_SMEAR) may have blank and duplicate IDs, which should be noted during comparison. 2. The infection (INFECTION) field in the smear test file is a multiple choice question; care must be taken when extracting for analysis.",
